SLASH local modification to the pinned QDMA submodule (libqdma).

libqdma: fix runtime writeback-interval updates

The QDMA_CSR_REG_UPDATE implementation passes the writeback-interval enum by
value to a HAL callback that requires a pointer. It also checks for active
queues using the PCI bus number instead of libqdma's device index, and the
CPM5 HAL ORs the new interval into the register without clearing the old field.
The feature is normally compiled out, which hides these defects.

Pass a local enum by address in both update paths and use the same device index
as the other global-CSR setters. Replace the CPM5 field rather than accumulating
its encoding. This allows SLASH to select the writeback interval during probe,
before any queues exist, without changing libqdma's default for other users.

Generated against qdma_drv @ 03ac7f3 (pinned submodule commit).
Applied automatically by driver/Makefile (libqdma-patches target, patch -p1).
